The Pokémon Trading Card Game (TCG) is a physical card game launched alongside the video game franchise. Players build decks and battle opponents using Pokémon cards, trainer cards, and energy cards. Matches involve drawing cards, playing Pokémon to the field, attaching energy, and using attacks. Only one Pokémon can attack per turn; defeated Pokémon are discarded. Players win by knocking out all opponent's Pokémon. The TCG experienced a massive resurgence in popularity during 2020s. Official resources include TCGplayer tutorials and YouTube guides. The game emphasizes strategy, deck-building, and competitive play alongside casual collecting. Cards feature artwork and come in varying rarity levels.